+matched runs, and bands show nearest-rank interquartile ranges. Empty fronts retain infinite
+distance scores and zero hypervolume; nonfinite aggregate distances appear as gaps. The
+hypervolume reference is the pooled-front nadir plus \SI{25}{\percent} of each coordinate span.
+These are metric histories, not interpolated objective-space Pareto fronts.}
+\label{fig:revision_quality}
+\end{figure}
+\begin{figure}[htbp]
